      "description": "Watch Brann vs Universitatea Cluj highlights and goals from UEFA Europa Conference League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 30, 2026. On a high-stakes evening in the UEFA Europa Conference League , Brann hosted Universitatea Cluj in a match filled with tactical intrigue and individual brilliance. Both sides entered the pitch on July 30, 2026, looking to seize control of this European tie under the lights. Castro Leads the Charge in an Explosive Opening The match ignited early as the home side wasted no time establishing their dominance. In the 8th minute, Niklas Castro found the back of the net following a pinpoint assist from Denzel De Roeve , sending the home crowd into raptures. The visitors from Universitatea Cluj refused to back down, showing their physical intent early on as Dino Mikanovic picked up a yellow card. Their persistence paid off in the 26th minute when Jovo Lukic struck a clinical equalizer to level the score at 1-1. As the first half progressed, the intensity remained high, with Niklas Castro entering the referee's book for a challenge in the 32nd minute. However, the forward quickly shifted his focus back to the attack. In the final minute of the half, Castro turned provider, setting up Ulrik Mathisen for a crucial goal that restored Brann 's lead just before the whistle. A yellow card for Marius Stefanescu moments later highlighted the growing frustration within the Romanian ranks. Second Half Dominance and Final Whistle The second half saw both managers turn to their benches to influence the flow of the game. Universitatea Cluj introduced Dan Nistor at the restart, but Brann continued to dictate the tempo. The decisive blow arrived in the 75th minute when Niklas Castro completed his brace, firing home to make it 3-1. The goal effectively broke the spirit of the visitors, who struggled to find a way back into the contest despite late tactical changes. The closing stages were characterized by defensive solidity from Brann and a flurry of bookings for the visitors, as Dorin Codrea and Alexandru Chipciu were cautioned. After five minutes of added time, the referee brought the encounter to a close. Brann walked off the pitch with a significant advantage to take into the second leg, thanks largely to the inspired performance of Niklas Castro ."
